{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q18344129","formula":"CH₅NO","hill":"CH5NO","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":1.0,"H":5.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Methoxyamine"},"descriptions":{"en":"Methoxyamine is the organic compound with the formula CH3ONH2. Also called O-methylhydroxylamine, it is a colourless volatile liquid that is soluble in polar organic solvent and in water. It is a derivative of hydroxylamine with the hydroxyl hydrogen replaced by a methyl group, an alkoxyamine.","ru":"Метоксиамин — органическое соединение с химической формулой CH3ONH2. Представляет собой бесцветную, летучую жидкость, растворимую в воде и полярных органических растворителях. Является производным гидроксиламина, в котором атом водорода гидроксильной группы замещён на метильную группу."},"fame":8,"pubchemCid":4113,"mass":47.057,"charge":0,"smiles":"CON","inchikey":"GMPKIPWJBDOURN-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"O-methylhydroxylamine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"4113","atoms":8,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.018,"y":-0.566,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.168,"y":0.277,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":1.151,"y":0.29,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":2.05,"y":-0.332,"z":0.0,"el":"H"},{"x":1.162,"y":0.915,"z":0.898,"el":"H"},{"x":1.162,"y":0.915,"z":-0.898,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.656,"y":-0.088,"z":0.817,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.656,"y":-0.088,"z":-0.817,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,1,1],[0,2,1],[1,6,1],[1,7,1],[2,3,1],[2,4,1],[2,5,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q18344129","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Methoxyamine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9C%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%BE%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%B8%D0%B0%D0%B